"PHASE 1 IMPLEMENTATION PLAN (2026-08-12, user gave the go). Scope: core stance machinery end to end; armament sets/loadout prep tables, forced-stance contests, relations/statuses, and quest acquisition remain later phases. Data model: (1) StatBlock small-int section gains property stats hand, gait, reach (i8; bladed/pole/etc. wait for equipment; size waits for contests). (2) StatRequirements: secador-stamped struct of Option<i8>/Option<i16> per int stat -- explicitly named thresholds, absent = unchecked (no zero-means-skip magic); StatBlock::meets(). Same type on wire and in assets (no name resolution inside). (3) Action rows + ActionAsset gain requirements: StatRequirements. (4) New asset kind Stance { id, name, requirements (to adopt), stat_block (contributions incl. granted action_ids -- reusing StatBlock id-vec) }; push enforces <=6 granted actions per stance. (5) ActiveStanceComponent { stance_id } with dirties(total_stat_block_dirty_flag); EntityBlobAsset.stance_name resolved at push. (6) entity_stats_system: base = baseline + traits cache + (placeholder equipment/status caches, now actually merged); total = base + active stance stat block; derived ActionsComponent = total.action_ids filtered by each action's requirements against total. Swapping stances or any stat change recomputes via existing dirty flags. (7) set_stance reducer: validates stance requirements against BASE (stance cannot provide to its own adoption); instant for now -- one-round swap cost lands with the loadout action in phase 2. Content: human baseline provides hand 2 gait 2 reach 1, slime gait 1, bat gait 2; move/quick_move require gait>=1, bop/boppity_bop require hand>=1; stances brawler (requires hand>=1), amorphous, prone (gait -2, attack -1, defense -1 -- swapping to prone visibly removes move: the demo of the whole pipeline). new_player blob gets brawler. Client: stances + active_stance_components subscribed, StancePanel lists stances w/ active highlight and swap via setStance, mocks extended. e2e phase 7-stances: derived actions, prone filtering, swap back, unmeetable-requirement rejection."